                <pb facs="0233" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/512: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-08-18T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>305. I am in entire accord with your point of view. I think Owen Young’s
                    appointment is highly desirable if it can be effected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
